{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Tunics of skin.</b> Rashi's comment: hides like a fingernail (smooth). That is to say, there was no hair on the skin, to exclude those who say it was rabbit skin, which is full of hair." "<b>Tunics of skin.</b> Rashi's comment: for the skin of their body and their flesh, as in 'it shall eat the parts of his skin' — the limbs of his body. And one should not explain it as the skin of an animal, for no animal had been flayed yet. And so Onkelos translated: למשך בשריהון (to envelop their flesh). Another interpretation: <b>tunics of skin</b> — from the skin of the Leviathan's mate, which the Holy One, blessed be He, slaughtered, and the salt that remains is kept for the righteous in the world to come." "<b>And He clothed them.</b> At first, 'and they made for themselves girdles' implies from the waist down; and in the end, <b>tunics of skin, and He clothed them</b> — over their entire body."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:50.170357585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}